## Reviewer
### Summary

The paper proposes a method to mitigate the task balancing problem in multi-task learning, which is a common problem where some tasks perform well but others perform unsatisfactorily. The method consists of two components: a loss-scale balancing method that ensures all task losses have the same scale via logarithmic transformation, and a gradient-magnitude balancing method that guarantees all task gradients have the same magnitude as the maximum gradient norm. The authors conduct experiments on several benchmark datasets and show that the proposed method outperforms existing methods in terms of performance improvement over single-task learning.

