- The paper is well-written and easy to follow. 
- The proposed method is simple and easy to implement. 
- The authors conduct extensive experiments on several benchmark datasets and show that the proposed method outperforms existing methods.

### Weaknesses

- The proposed method is an extension of the existing method, IMTL. The authors only use the loss balancing method of IMTL and replace the gradient balancing method of IMTL with their own method. 
- The authors do not provide any theoretical analysis of the proposed method. 
- The authors do not provide any analysis of the computational cost of the proposed method. 
- The authors do not provide any analysis of the convergence of the proposed method. 

### Questions

- The authors claim that the logarithmic transformation is equivalent to IMTL-L when $s_t$ is the exact minimizer in each iteration. However, the minimizer $s_t$ is not guaranteed to be exact in practice. How does the proposed method compare to IMTL-L in this case? 
